    fix(graph): scope-gate coverage-links, test-classes and rollup to the Hilo repo itself (Addresses DF-WARPFS-159)
    
    The COV chain (graph surfaces -> coverage-links -> test-classes -> rollup)
    models the Hilo repository itself only (GAP-112). On a warmed foreign tree the
    downstream commands used to fail on a missing .vfs/graph artifact and point
    the user at `hilo graph surfaces` — a command that refuses on that very tree.
    Each downstream run() now takes the shared require_self_scope precondition
    before reading any artifact and refuses with the self-only limitation named;
    planted foreign artifacts are never touched. Completes the prior surfaces.rs
    work (helper + shared scope fixtures), fixing the helper's non-Display Path
    format; the two cli.rs fixtures that exercise downstream COV logic through
    the compiled binary now plant the GAP-112 self markers; docs/cli-reference.md
    documents the shared gate.
    
